    "io_mode": "stdin",
    "statement": "## Unicode Matchday Repeats\n\nA scoreboard stores one UTF-8 banner `S`. Officials index it by **League Graphemes**, while broadcasts use UTF-16 code-unit offsets.\n\nThe beginning and end of `S` are grapheme boundaries. For each internal gap between adjacent Unicode scalar values, apply the first matching rule:\n\n1. Between U+000D and U+000A, there is no boundary.\n2. If either scalar is a control, there is a boundary. Controls are U+0000..U+001F and U+007F..U+009F.\n3. If the right scalar is an Attachment or U+200D, there is no boundary.\n4. If the left scalar is U+200D, the right scalar is an Emoji, and the nearest scalar before that U+200D after skipping Attachments is an Emoji, there is no boundary.\n5. If both scalars are Regional Indicators, count the consecutive Regional Indicators ending at the left scalar. There is no boundary exactly when that count is odd.\n6. Otherwise, there is a boundary.\n\nAttachment ranges are U+0300..U+036F, U+1AB0..U+1AFF, U+1DC0..U+1DFF, U+20D0..U+20FF, U+FE00..U+FE0F, U+FE20..U+FE2F, U+1F3FB..U+1F3FF, and U+E0100..U+E01EF. Emoji ranges are U+2600..U+27BF and U+1F000..U+1FAFF. Regional Indicators are U+1F1E6..U+1F1FF. Classes may overlap; rule order is aut",
    "deadline_s": 300.0,
